From: BE-IIS <info@be-iis.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: max96717: honor low GPIO output values

The GPIO set callback currently ignores its value argument and always writes
MAX96717_GPIO_OUT. As a result, a GPIO can be set high but cannot subsequently
be cleared through gpiolib.

Use the requested value when updating the GPIO output bit.

This is a local BE-IIS fix pending upstream submission and review.

---
 max96717.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- max96717.c
+++ max96717.c
@@ -302,8 +302,9 @@ static void max96717_gpiochip_set(struct gpio_chip *gpiochip,
 	struct max96717_priv *priv = gpiochip_get_data(gpiochip);
 
 	cci_update_bits(priv->regmap, MAX96717_GPIO_REG_A(offset),
-			MAX96717_GPIO_OUT, MAX96717_GPIO_OUT, NULL);
+			MAX96717_GPIO_OUT,
+			value ? MAX96717_GPIO_OUT : 0, NULL);
 }
 
 static int max96717_gpio_get_direction(struct gpio_chip *gpiochip,
